[{:db/id "q-275757/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5fab8c5b-110a-5f53-b3c9-4fd77954da68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275757/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "392b40d0-742a-5201-9772-387ceac68044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275757/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "abc3316d-4bab-54f5-aa83-c84a92afd041" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275757/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-275757/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-275757/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275757" :question/id #uuid "f1605a7c-6610-56ff-a112-240e6e5bbd01" :question/math-academy-id "q-275757" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2+k)-(-4+2)-(2k+2) \\\\  & =2+k+2-2k-2 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ -1\\cdot (k-2) & =2 \\\\ k-2 & =-2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275757/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275757"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319409/field-1/fd9e7a740343f6f85c50219552c3c4e2bc9558e9c34cb9f4697cfbd10f2c3da0" :answer/id #uuid "f9092226-c93b-564e-8674-90cdda0e56fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319409/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "50ec604c-1d1b-5e6c-8052-8a4b3e24aec1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319409/field-1/fd9e7a740343f6f85c50219552c3c4e2bc9558e9c34cb9f4697cfbd10f2c3da0" :answer-field/choices ["q-319409/field-1/fd9e7a740343f6f85c50219552c3c4e2bc9558e9c34cb9f4697cfbd10f2c3da0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319409" :question/id #uuid "3e46c518-3e5c-53ed-8495-f09dea2fdfbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-319409" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319409/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
